."],"id":"44704074-0ee1-45d1-a1f3-1306e296f92c"},{"links":[["ruined","ruined"],["dilapidated","dilapidated"]],"glosses":["Characterized by ruin; ruined; dilapidated; as, an edifice, bridge, or wall in a ruinous state."],"id":"f3a17334-73b0-4fcb-9343-6fb068e346e5"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"characterized by ruin","word":"ramshackle"}]},"ruination":{"id":"4dca640f-b29e-4c09-89ea-48d894da8e75","word":"ruination","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"state of being ruined","word":"ruína"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"act of ruining","word":"ruína"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"As our tour has shown, the state of ruination of castle sites was a key factor in their fate when the railways came through.","ref":"2022 January 12, Dr. Joseph Brennan, “Castles: ruined and redeemed by rail”, in RAIL, number 948, page 56:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[36,45]],"id":"88206262-9dbc-4ae9-a752-696d777a2225"}],"links":[["ruin","ruin"],["devastation","devastation"],["destruction","destruction"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["The state of being ruined, a state of devastation or destruction."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"83056377-17d3-472a-8fd0-fe175cb3b6b6"},{"links":[["wreck","wreck"]],"glosses":["The act of ruining or wrecking."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"6b843003-8b07-4917-8bc0-0d13f759c838"},{"links":[["destroy","destroy"],["lost","lost"]],"glosses":["The cause of being ruined, destroyed or lost."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"c19150e5-6de0-4b86-ba9d-668b6e0cb345"},{"examples":[{"text":"Yet also thanks largely to Trump, a parallel disaster is unfolding across the world: the ruination of America’s reputation as a safe, trustworthy, competent international leader and partner.","ref":"2020 April 12, Simon Tisdall, “US's global reputation hits rock-bottom over Trump's coronavirus response”, in The Guardian:","t